keywords:
  - systemic sclerosis
  - scleroderma
  - single nuclei multiome
  - snATAC-seq
  - dissociation bias
  - cell type composition
  - GSE312129
abstract: >-
  Reprocessing of GSE312129, the only public paired multiome of systemic
  sclerosis skin, finds that fibroblast nuclei are recovered from SSc skin at
  roughly one sixth the rate of healthy skin, in the direction opposite to the
  disease. The asymmetry is corroborated by COL1A1 detection and is a
  composition confound for any between-group comparison drawn from this
  dataset. Also included is the complete record of the preregistered RUNX
  paralog analysis that did not reach its donor floor and was stopped.
notes: >-
  Author order and creator format match the Ritschel Research house convention used
  across its Zenodo deposits.

